Hook payloads an agent sends to `adj hook claude`, read by `src/transport/cli/hook/tests.rs` and
`tests/agent_sessions.rs`. One file per event:

    session-start.json                 SessionStart
    user-prompt-submit.json            UserPromptSubmit
    post-tool-use.json                 PostToolUse, an Edit
    post-tool-use-failure.json         PostToolUseFailure, a Bash command
    permission-request.json            PermissionRequest
    permission-request-ask-user-question.json
                                       PermissionRequest for AskUserQuestion (a question, no command)
    notification-permission.json       Notification, permission_prompt
    notification-idle.json             Notification, idle_prompt
    subagent-start.json                SubagentStart
    subagent-post-tool-use.json        PostToolUse sent by a sub-agent (carries agent_id)
    subagent-permission-request.json   PermissionRequest sent by a sub-agent
    subagent-stop.json                 SubagentStop
    stop.json                          Stop
    stop-failure.json                  StopFailure
    session-end.json                   SessionEnd
    status-line.json                   the status line's stdin (`adj hook claude --status-line`), not a hook

Recorded from a real session (Claude Code 2.1.291, `claude -p` with a hand-written `--settings`
file whose hooks wrote their stdin to a file): the keys of `session-start.json` and
`user-prompt-submit.json`, of `stop.json` as far as they were noted (`stop_hook_active`,
`last_assistant_message`, the common ones), and the whole of `subagent-start.json`,
`subagent-post-tool-use.json` (a sub-agent's Bash call) and `subagent-stop.json`, from a session
that had a sub-agent run `ls`. A sub-agent's events carry `agent_id` and `agent_type`; its
`PostToolUse` also carries `effort`.

Recorded on Claude Code 2.1.292 (same method): `permission-request-ask-user-question.json`, the
`PermissionRequest` Claude Code sends when the model asks a question with the `AskUserQuestion`
tool. Its `tool_input` holds `questions`, not a command or a path.

Written by hand from the Claude Code hooks reference, with the keys it lists for the event (and
`prompt_id` and `duration_ms`, which the recorded tool events carry): both `notification-*.json`,
`post-tool-use.json` (an Edit), `post-tool-use-failure.json`, `permission-request.json`,
`stop-failure.json`, `session-end.json` and `subagent-permission-request.json` (the recorded
sub-agent layout with a permission request's keys), and `status-line.json` (the keys of the
status line input the Claude Code documentation lists). The recorded session asked for no permission
and ran no tool of its own that fails. When one is recorded, replace the hand-written file.

Editing applied, since the repository is public: the session id, the prompt id, the agent id and the tool use id
became fixed values, paths became `/home/user/...`, and the prompt and message text was made plain.
Each recorded file keeps the keys the binary sent.

The tests rewrite `cwd` to the fixture repository and `session_id` where they need more than one
session; nothing else is edited.
